not hold. In the pooled contrasts, either P or G alone accounts for most of the measured reduction;
adding the other contributes little. The pattern also appears in the fixed-attack contrasts averaged
over the eight selected attacks (P: −0.087). Our registered conjectures (P negligible, the targeting
parts additive, S helpful) failed as scored (Table 22); the stricter eligibility reading of Table 21 leaves
them not assessed, with the estimates unchanged. X7-SC agrees (Table 12).

Stronger attacks and where R3 fails (Q3). Table 15 gives each core rule’s attack envelope:
the family with the highest training gain, evaluated unchanged. These are finite-search results,
not bounds on the families. Against
