only. A nesting comparison on the existing records (exploratory) shows evaluation discrepancies that
call for further search checks, also in unflagged cells: X7-SC contains D2+H3, yet in 6 of 21 cells the
X7-SC winner’s evaluated gain falls short of the better of the frozen and doubled D2+H3 winners
on the same seeds by more than the doubling threshold (at most 0.021). Winners are selected on
training seeds and need not keep their order on evaluation seeds, and picking the better D2+H3
winner on the evaluation seeds favours it, so this is a discrepancy, not a demonstrated search failure.
The report lists the search-flagged cells, and the addendum traces the inherited flags of every Q1 and
Q4 decision through the records’ references. Q2 and Q3 statements are descriptive; the cells they
use carry the flags listed in the report. Table 19 sets the Q1 estimates beside their re-evaluation with
