(under D2+H3 with the doubled searches, and with each rule’s strongest family, it is positive on
all six), and this analysis does not establish the ordering for the neighbourhood. At the headline
market, the selected unconstrained welfare attacks yield gross efficiency of about 0.840 against all
three core rules and earn less than the truthful reference against R3 and C∗ . The registered W1
search found no profitable welfare attack (gross efficiency near 0.997); exploratory mixtures of a
welfare attack and a profitable attack reach lower efficiency at non-negative estimated gain, so it
supplies no efficiency bound for randomised policies. These conclusions concern frozen searches and
references, with interval calibration admitted on development fixtures. The record of both tests,
including the original failure, the amendments, the deviations, and the failed predictions, will be
released with the paper.

